# ============================================================
#  Expansion — more generic relationship events (actor: any).
# ============================================================

@event soc_lost_notes
title: The Borrowed Notes
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where (tagged(npc, student) or tagged(npc, prefect)) and rel(npc) >= 3
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: scroll
tags: social study
scene: A student holding a single soggy page of notes, the rest of the stack floating away down a stream behind them.
text: {npc} borrowed all your lecture notes last week. {They} {are} now standing in front of you holding a single soggy page. "There was a stream," {they} say{s}. "And a duck. Mostly a duck."
> left: Laugh it off
  rel npc +medium
  study -tiny
  say: You rewrite your notes from memory. {npc} brings you a cake every day for a week, by way of apology. The cakes are better than the notes were.
> right: Make {them} rewrite them
  rel npc -tiny
  study +tiny
  say: {npc} copies out forty pages from a friend's notes, grumbling. The new notes are neater than yours ever were.

@event soc_birthday
title: A Birthday
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 9
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 12
art: gem
tags: social festival
scene: A small cake with a single candle in a dark common room, a group of students crouched behind a sofa, a surprised face in the doorway.
text: {&You find out — by accident — that it's {npc}'s birthday. {They} haven't told anyone. {They} {are} spending it in the library, alone, on purpose.|It's {npc}'s birthday again, and again {they} haven't told anyone. {They} {are} in the library, alone, as if you might have forgotten.}
> left: Organise a surprise
  gold -small
  rel npc +large
  mood +small
  say: {&Seven people jump out from behind a sofa. {npc} screams, then laughs, then has to sit down. "How did you know?" You'll never tell.|This year it's a cake shaped, badly, like the library. {npc} pretends to be annoyed for nearly a minute.}
> right: Join {them} in the library
  rel npc +medium
  lore +tiny
  say: {&You sit down opposite {them} with your own book.|You take the same seat as last year, with your own book.} Neither of you says happy birthday. At midnight {they} slide{s} a biscuit across the table, and you both grin.

@event soc_bad_news
title: Bad News From Home
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where (tagged(npc, student) or tagged(npc, prefect)) and rel(npc) >= 12
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 12
art: letter
tags: social
scene: A student sitting on a stone staircase with a crumpled letter, head bowed, a friend sitting down beside them.
text: {npc} is sitting on the stairs with a letter in {their} lap, not moving. {Their} grandmother is ill. The barge home takes two days. "I don't know whether to go," {they} say{s}.
> left: "Go. We'll cover your classes."
  rel npc +large
  study -tiny
  say: {npc} catches the next barge. Every evening you copy out the day's notes for {them} from {their} classmates. When {npc} comes back, {their} grandmother is better, and {they} hug{s} you on the landing.
> right: Just sit with {them}
  rel npc +medium
  mood -tiny
  say: You sit there until the stairs move under you. You don't fix anything. That's not what {they} needed.

@event soc_stargazing
title: Counting Stars
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and rel(npc) >= 12 and bond(npc) != "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: star
tags: social romance
scene: Two students lying on their backs on a flat roof, close but not quite touching, a sky full of stars above.
text: {&{npc} has dragged a blanket up to the roof.|{npc} is on the roof again with the blanket, and a flask this time.|{npc} has found a better spot on the roof, out of the wind, and a better blanket.} "There's a meteor shower," {they} say{s}. "Supposedly." There's room on the blanket for two, just about.
> left: Count meteors
  health -tiny
  rel npc +medium
  mood +small
  say: You count thirty-one. {npc} counts thirty-four and accuses you of not looking properly. You weren't, entirely. You stay until the cold drives you in at dawn.
> right: Talk about everything else
  health -tiny
  spark npc +small
  rel npc +small
  say: You don't see a single meteor. You talk about home and fear and what you'd do if you could do anything. When you look up, the sky's gone grey with dawn.

@event soc_jealous_friend
title: Jealousy
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and (bond(npc) == "friend" or bond(npc) == "close")
per: npc
trigger: social
when: known() >= 4
repeat: 10
art: mask
tags: social
scene: A student standing alone at the edge of a laughing group, arms folded, watching someone else take what used to be their seat.
text: {~{npc} has been odd all week. Finally it comes out.|{npc} has been short with you at every meal. Finally, on the stairs, it comes out.|{npc} cancels on you twice and then turns up at your door. It comes out in a rush.} "You've got all these new friends now. I just — I don't know where I fit anymore."
> left: Reassure {them}
  rel npc +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: You tell {them} exactly where {they} fit: right here, first. {npc} rolls {their} eyes, but {they}'re smiling. The oddness is gone by dinner.
> right: Tell {them} friendship isn't a contest
  rel npc -tiny
  lore +tiny
  say: You're right, technically. {npc} knows it. It still lands badly. It takes a few weeks for things to feel easy again. You spend the evenings you'd have spent soothing {them} in the library instead.

@event soc_teach_spell
title: A Trick Worth Learning
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 7
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: wand
tags: social magic
scene: Two students in an empty classroom, one demonstrating a wand movement, the other copying it with a tiny spark of light.
text: {npc} has a spell {they} invented — a little thing, half-useful, half-ridiculous — and wants to teach it to someone. {&"It makes your tea exactly the right temperature," {they} say{s}. "Forever."|"It finds the page you were reading," {they} say{s}. "Any book, anywhere."|"It keeps your socks dry," {they} say{s}. "Lake, rain, puddles. Dry."}
> left: Learn it properly
  chance likely:
    arcana +small
    rel npc +small
    say: It takes an hour. {&Your tea is now perfect, always.|You will never lose your page again.|Your socks are dry. Your socks will always be dry.} You'll use this spell more than anything you learn in class.
  else:
    health -tiny
    rel npc +small
    say: {&The first attempt freezes your tea solid, and your eyebrows with it. The second works. Your eyebrows take a day to thaw.|The first attempt finds every page in the library at once. The second works. The librarian is not amused.|The first attempt dries your socks, your shoes and most of your feet. The second works. Your skin flakes for a day.}
> right: Teach {them} one of yours in return
  rel npc +medium
  charm +tiny
  say: You trade spells like secrets. By midnight you've both got a new trick and an inside joke that will last three years.

@event soc_secret_admirer
title: A Secret Admirer
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and spark(npc) >= 15 and bond(npc) != "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
art: letter
tags: romance
scene: A folded note tucked into a library book with a pressed flower, unsigned, the handwriting careful and slightly shaky.
text: Folded notes keep appearing in your library books. Unsigned. They're funny, and a little nervous, and they know things about you that only someone paying attention would know. The handwriting looks familiar.
> left: Leave a note back
  spark npc +small
  say: You write back. The notes get longer. One day the last line just says: "It's {npc}. You knew, didn't you?" You did.
> right: Stake out the library
  challenge deceive apprentice:
    win:
      spark npc +medium
      rel npc +small
      say: You catch {npc} red-handed, mid-tuck. {They} turn{s} the colour of a pyromancy exam. You both laugh until the librarian throws you out.
    lose:
      spark npc +tiny
      say: You wait three nights and catch nobody. On the fourth morning the note says: "Nice try."

@event soc_injured_friend
title: Carried
class: routine
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and rel(npc) >= 6
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 10
art: cross
tags: social danger
scene: A student carrying another piggyback across a muddy lawn, the injured one's ankle wrapped in a scarf.
text: {npc} has twisted an ankle on the far side of the grounds, a long way from the infirmary, and it's getting dark. {They} {are} trying very hard to pretend it doesn't hurt.
> left: Carry {them} on your back
  vigor +small
  rel npc +medium
  health -tiny
  alignment +tiny
  say: It's a long way. {npc} narrates the whole journey like a horse race. By the time you reach the infirmary you're both laughing too hard to breathe.
> right: Run for help
  rel npc +small
  say: You run for Sister Amaranth, who arrives with a floating stretcher and a lot of opinions. {npc} is fine. {They} send{s} you a thank-you sweet.

@event soc_rival_decency
title: An Unexpected Kindness
class: routine
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, peer) and (bond(npc) == "rival" or bond(npc) == "nemesis" or rel(npc) <= -9)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 10
art: hand
tags: rival social
scene: A student picking up a rival's scattered books from a wet floor, the rival frozen mid-step, not sure what to say.
text: {&You drop your books in the rain, and the first person to stoop and help pick them up is {npc}.|You slip on the wet stairs, and the hand that catches your elbow is {npc}'s.|The wind off the lake takes your scarf, and {npc} is the one who runs after it.} {They} hand{s} it back without a word, looking as surprised as you are.
> left: Thank {them} properly
  rel npc +large
  say: "Don't make it a thing," {npc} mutters. But the next day {they} nod{s} to you in the corridor. {&Something has thawed.|It's getting harder to stay enemies.|You're not sure what you are to each other anymore.}
> right: Suspect a trick
  rel npc -tiny
  guile +tiny
  say: You check for hexes. There aren't any. {npc} saw you checking. You'll both remember that.

@event soc_partner_anniversary
title: An Anniversary
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner" and spark(npc) >= 40
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 12
art: ring
tags: romance
scene: Two people on a bench by the lake at sunset, one holding out a small wrapped box, the other's hands over their mouth.
text: It's been a while now — long enough that {npc} has started calling things "ours". Today {they} hand{s} you a small wrapped box and won't meet your eyes.
> left: Open it now
  spark npc +small
  mood +medium
  say: Inside: a pebble from the lakeshore, polished to a shine, from the day you first really talked. "It's stupid," {npc} says. It isn't. You carry it everywhere, and spend the next day hunting for something half as good to give back.
> right: Give {them} yours first
  gold -small
  spark npc +medium
  mood +medium
  say: You'd had the same idea, and spent most of your purse on it. You both open your boxes at once. They're nearly the same gift. You laugh until the sun goes down.
